  - modified gravity
  - infrared screening
  - Energy-Flow Cosmology
abstract: >-
  We test the cosmological viability of a discrete entropic gravity operator
  exhibiting Newtonian and MOND-like regimes with Λ-locked infrared screening.
  The effective gravitational coupling G_eff(k,a) is embedded into the linear
  growth equation for matter perturbations. Three scenarios are compared:
  Λ-locked transition at super-Hubble scale (4.4 Gpc), at 10 Mpc, and at
  1 Mpc. Only Λ-locking preserves realistic structure growth (σ₈ ≈ 0.8).
  Any sub-Hubble transition scale leads to catastrophic overgrowth (σ₈ >> 1),
  establishing Λ-locking as a necessary condition for cosmological consistency.
